"""ycash-bootstrap: restore a checkpoint bundle into an empty datadir (testnet plan §4.4).

    ycash-bootstrap --network testnet-yb-fast --datadir DIR [--source URL|DIR] [--reset] [--verify-full]
    ycash-bootstrap --network main --datadir DIR --source https://snapshots.ycash.team/main/latest/
    ycash-bootstrap --network regtest --datadir DIR --pack OUT --last-height N   # make a regtest bundle

Two layers (§4.0). The **prefix** (the default): Zcash testnet blocks 0..510,247 in the frozen
format `ycash-prefix/1` (ycash-infra `bundles/prefix/FORMAT.md`), shared by the three testnets
because it carries no network magic. The **state bundle** (`--state --source DIR|URL`): a ycash6
datadir at a height H above the fork in the format `ycash-state/1` (the testnets), `ycash-state/2`
or `ycash-state/3` (mainnet: one tarball, or the same stream in parts of 1 GiB; ycash-infra
`bundles/state/FORMAT.md`), checked against its statements (below the prefix steps). Mainnet
(`--network main`) takes a state bundle only.

Restoring, in order, refusing at the first failure:
  1. the target network's subdirectory (`testnet-yb-fast`, ...) must hold no chain yet; `--reset`
     first moves an existing wallet.dat aside and removes that subdirectory (testnet resets, T-7);
  2. `SHA256SUMS` is fetched; its own sha256 must equal the value this release pins for the
     network (the profile's `prefix.sha256sums_sha256`); a `SHA256SUMS.minisig` beside it must
     verify with the owner's key (keys/ycash-release.pub; optional until the bundle is signed,
     mandatory with `--require-signature`);
  3. `manifest.json` must match its sum and the release: format, network, the chunk rule, the
     last height and hash (= the compiled checkpoint), the compiled earlier checkpoints;
  4. every chunk is downloaded and checked against `SHA256SUMS` and the manifest, then framed for
     `-loadblock` with the network's magic (`<magic> <LE u32 length> <block>`), checking the hash
     chain, the genesis, every manifest hash, the raw size and sha256 on the way;
  5. `ycashd` imports the framed files with `-connect=0 -listen=0 -disablewallet` (so a wallet is
     created, from -mnemonicfile or not, only at the node's first normal start; and `-checkpoints=0` under
     `--verify-full`, which validates every block's scripts instead of trusting the checkpoint), reading
     a copy of ycash.conf without its peer settings (addnode, connect, seednode, listen, bind, ...:
     the conf adds to the command line's -connect=0, it does not yield to it); a peer at any poll fails it;
  6. the node must reach the last height with `getblockhash` equal to the manifest at every listed
     height and to the compiled checkpoint at the last; then it is stopped and the framed files
     are removed. Start the node normally afterwards.

A state bundle, in order: a source ending in `latest/` is read for its height only and re-based to
`../<H>/`; SHA256SUMS and its signature (always required on mainnet, where `--allow-unsigned` is
refused; required for a state bundle over http(s), where `--allow-unsigned` accepts an unsigned one,
loudly); the canonical manifest (format, the network and
-testnetprofile, line ycash6, H above the fork, the compiled pins, the tarball or its parts against
SHA256SUMS); the statements (v1: at least two, byte-identical; v2/v3: statement-ycash6.json) and
treestate.json against their lines; free disk for the restore. Then the parts (a v1/v2 tarball is
one part) are fetched one at a time, each checked against its signed size and sha256 before any of
its bytes reaches the extractor, resumed with an HTTP Range request after a broken download, and
deleted once extracted, so the restore needs one part of extra disk. One streaming extraction
writes directories and regular files under `<network>/{blocks,chainstate,vaults,yellowback}` only
(no wallet, no LevelDB LOCK/LOG, no links) into DATADIR/.bootstrap-staging; at the end of the
stream its size, sha256 and tree hash must equal the manifest's, and only then are the directories
moved into the network's directory (mainnet: the datadir itself). Then the node starts offline,
settles, rolls back with `invalidateblock H+1` when it connected blocks above H, must produce the
statement's fields itself (getblockhash, chainwork, gettxoutsetinfo, vault_getinfo,
yed_getstatehash; v2: getblock's finalsaplingroot and chain supply) and every pin, and
`reconsiderblock`s. A failure removes what was extracted or installed.

A restore that changes the datadir first writes DATADIR/<network>.bootstrap-incomplete and removes it
only when it has succeeded: a refused, failed or killed restore leaves it behind, with the reason,
and the image entrypoint (contrib/docker/ycashd) does not start ycashd while it is there. Exit
status: 0 restored, 2 refused (the message and the marker say why).

Nothing in a bundle is executed; file names are checked against the format before they become a
path or a URL. Python standard library only (plus the `minisign` binary when a signature is
present); run it with `python3 -I`.
"""

